+    // LokLM patch: skip the prebuilt-binary self-test ONLY inside our Electron
+    // utility-process models worker. node-llama-cpp runs this test by forking a
+    // child process; in a utility process that child (a plain Node fork) can't
+    // load node-llama-cpp's deps from inside app.asar, so the test always fails
+    // and node-llama-cpp silently falls back to the CPU binary — the GPU is
+    // never used in packaged builds. By the time the worker attempts a GPU
+    // binary, the Electron MAIN process has already validated it (its GPU probe
+    // is what lets the worker's placement be GPU at all), so skipping the test
+    // there is safe. We MUST keep the test everywhere else (main process,
+    // node-llama-cpp's postinstall, machines with no/incompatible GPU driver):
+    // without it, loading a GPU binary directly aborts the process with
+    // vk::IncompatibleDriverError instead of falling back to CPU. The Electron
+    // utility process is the only context with `process.parentPort`.
+    if (typeof process !== "undefined" && process.parentPort != null)
+        return false;
     if (platform === "linux") {
         if (isPrebuiltBinary)
             return true;
